# .mailmap — canonical contributor identities
#
# ZD-W2-04 · diligence. `git log` across the estate yields 41 distinct author
# identities for roughly 28 people. Section 4 of the diligence checklist (IP
# Ownership) needs a contributor list that a reviewer can act on, and 41
# strangers is not that — the same person appears as a personal address, a
# GitHub noreply alias, and sometimes a laptop hostname.
#
# This file is presentation only. It changes what `git log` DISPLAYS; it does
# not rewrite history, alter a commit, or change authorship of anything. It is
# the technical input to Pedro's IP assignment register, not a substitute for
# it: every person below still needs a signed agreement.
#
# Verify with:
#     git log --format='%aN <%aE>' --all | sort -u | wc -l
#
# Identical in every in-scope repository so the register is one list, not 12.
#
